== kodiak/grizzly thread (4804712) ==
[B]Update 2026-10-18: weekly Evolution X sync[/B]

New builds for both phones in this thread:
[LIST]
[*][B]Pixel 11 Pro XL (kodiak):[/B] [ICODE]EvolutionX-17.0-20261018-kodiak-12.3-Unofficial-fastboot.zip[/ICODE]
    SHA-256 [ICODE]0dd2e184a1a61518e3b333c3072d8ca48d7fb724366e2505f75e09a567656156[/ICODE]
    [URL=https://sourceforge.net/projects/denson9874-s-user-builds/files/kodiak/17/]SourceForge: kodiak/17[/URL]
[*][B]Pixel 11 Pro (grizzly):[/B] [ICODE]EvolutionX-17.0-20261018-grizzly-12.3-Unofficial-fastboot.zip[/ICODE]
    SHA-256 [ICODE]5e971deabeb379bf25408d12489aa07eed1b0d1dd33261b2b76b09c91ca276ac[/ICODE]
    [URL=https://sourceforge.net/projects/denson9874-s-user-builds/files/grizzly/17/]SourceForge: grizzly/17[/URL]
[/LIST]

[B]Already on the 2026-10-16 build?[/B] Settings > System > System updates has this one: it installs to the other slot in the background, then asks you to restart. Rooted with Magisk? Don't restart from there: Magisk > Install > [I]Install to inactive slot (after OTA)[/I] keeps root. Coming from an older build: [ICODE]fastboot update <zip>[/ICODE] (keeps your data).

[B]Changes (upstream Evolution X, October 9 to 18)[/B]
[LIST]
[*]Google apps updated from Pixel 11 Pro firmware CD1A.261005.003.
[*]Android System WebView 155.0.8059.39.
[*]Evolver: the spoofing settings are redesigned in Material 3 Expressive.
[*]Bluetooth no longer turns itself back on by default (auto-on is off).
[*]Mobile network: when a network scan is rejected, the phone falls back to the cells it can see.
[*]Bug reports include the full kernel log.
[*]Emergency information: picking a photo works without a crop app.
[*]Translation updates across Evolution X and LineageOS apps.
[/LIST]
[B]Known issue:[/B] a user has reported that Now Playing won't turn on in this build. It's being looked into.

Unchanged: Espada kernel v3 (Linux 6.12.92) by Kevtrejo37, Extreme Charging, the charging screensaver, "Use device MAC" for Wi-Fi networks that filter by MAC address (since the 10-16 build), and the stock CD1A.261005.003 firmware (security patch 2026-10-05). Fresh installs: see the first post.

